{
	title: 'Spawn and wait: subagents',
	spec: "A `spawn` tool (one file under src/host/tools/; named spawn, not spawn_agent, and its texts talk of sessions, not agents) opens a session next to the caller: kind `subagent` (sends a handoff to its parent with send, then its tab closes after a clean finish), `subagent-leave-open` (hands off, tab stays open), or `interactive` (a session for the user; blank without a task). Options as the old spawn_agent: task, mode fresh or fork (fork copies the parent's history so far), model, cwd, name, limit (spawn slots passed on; the parent spends limit+1, a slot never comes back; the first session has 5). The child exists and is working when spawn returns, so a `wait` later in the same round sees it: the old Hal queued the spawn through IPC and wait often ran first, answering 'nothing to wait for'. `wait` ends the caller's turn until the next subagent's handoff arrives, or says at once that none is running. A human prompt to a subagent keeps its tab open. The child's first prompt comes from its parent (task for senders), states its parent, slot budget and the handoff duty. Artifacts: old-spawn_agent.ts, old-wait.ts, old-runtime-excerpt.ts (spawn prompt, spawnSession, auto-close, promotion on a human prompt).",
	status: 'done',
